<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herius Asinius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 90 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herius Asinius was a commander of the Marrucini, an Italic people of the Adriatic coast, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-war-91-87-bce">Social War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He led his people's forces on the side of the Italian allies and was killed in battle in 90 BCE. He was the grandfather of the Roman statesman and historian Gaius Asinius Pollio.</p></div>
